Author: missingbulb <73882448+missingbulb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Sep 11 19:10:19 2026 +0300

    update: run the repo's own tests in the apply stage, reuse the open PR, and predict its shape (#1933)

    * update: run the repo's own tests in the apply stage, and predict the PR's shape

    The update's deterministic half gates on `selftest --strict` — Claudinite's own
    probes — and never the member's test suite. A cycle that rewrote engine code, a
    config key, or a repo source file through a migration merged green while the
    repo's tests were red.

    `converge-scope.mjs` reads what the cycle actually wrote out of the working tree
    and reports the paths a member's suite could see: everything but the vendored
    pack trees, the mount's own wiring, and a settings edit that moved only the
    installed stamp. A non-empty answer raises the apply stage, whose brief now
    carries the section that runs those tests and repairs what the update broke.

    `update`'s automerge stops being `anything` and becomes the prediction of that
    diff: the mount, the config files, `.github/workflows/` — what the apply stage
    delivers out of staging — and the test tree. A migration that rewrites a
    repo-owned source file lands outside it and parks the PR for a person.

    Refs #1932

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016osoLg3HdoVsPJ2cBucEoR

    * update: size the apply stage's bound to the suite it now runs

    Read against `writing-tasks` after the fact: task.md restated how the
    deterministic half gates rather than the constraint the session is under, the
    30-minute bound predated the stage running a whole test suite and repairing it,
    and the policy's two mount terms read as redundant with nothing saying why.

    Refs #1932

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016osoLg3HdoVsPJ2cBucEoR

    * update: reuse the open update PR rather than superseding it

    `supersede_existing_pr` cut a fresh branch every cycle and closed the last one,
    so a member that could not land accumulated an obsolete update PR a night. The
    task now declares `amend_existing_or_create_new_pr`: the converge is a full
    recompute from the base, so a cycle that finds its own open PR force-pushes that
    branch to this cycle's answer and rewrites the PR's title and body with it.

    The worker learns the two things that come with the declaration. It delivers onto
    `CLAUDINITE_TARGET_PR` where that PR is still open — it used to ignore the
    variable and unconditionally POST, which an amend target answers with a 422 — and
    a named PR closed under the run still opens a fresh one, since a push onto a
    closed PR delivers nothing while reporting a delivery.

    And it no longer pushes a tree the branch already carries. The converge recomputes
    the same answer nightly; a force-push would give the PR a new head and discard the
    checks already run on it, which on a member waiting for slow CI is the difference
    between eventually landing and never landing.

    Closes #1934

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016osoLg3HdoVsPJ2cBucEoR

    ---------

    Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

